{"slug":"boomerang-triples","title":"Equal Distances From a Point","topic":"hashing","difficulty":"medium","order":250,"tags":["hashing","hash-map","geometry","counting"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"For each centre, group the other points by distance","body":["Count ordered triples `(i, j, k)` of different points where the distance from `i` to `j` equals the distance from `i` to `k`. Fix the point `i` as the **centre**. Compute the squared distance to every other point (squared, so that no square roots or decimals are needed) and count in a map how many points have each distance.",{"code":"for each centre i:\n    d = {}\n    for each other point j:\n        dist = (xj - xi) ** 2 + (yj - yi) ** 2\n        d[dist] = d.get(dist, 0) + 1\n    for c in d.values():\n        total += c * (c - 1)       # ordered pairs (j, k) among c points"},"If `c` points have the same distance from the centre, there are `c * (c - 1)` ordered pairs `(j, k)` of different points among them. The work is `n` rounds of `n` map operations: O(n^2) instead of the `n^3` triples."]},"statement":["Given `n` different points with integer coordinates, count the ordered triples `(i, j, k)` of three different points such that the distance from point `i` to point `j` equals the distance from point `i` to point `k`. Triples with the same points in a different order are different triples."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`.","Each of the next `n` lines has the coordinates `x` and `y` of a point."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of triples."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 600","-10^4 <= x, y <= 10^4","All points are different."],"examples":[{"input":"3\n0 0\n1 0\n2 0\n","output":"2\n","note":"Only the middle point (1, 0) works as the centre: the other two points are both at distance 1, in two orders."}],"hints":["Use the squared distance, so everything stays an integer.","Fix a centre and count the points at each distance with a map.","Each distance with `c` points gives `c * (c - 1)` ordered pairs."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\npts = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(n)]\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <unordered_map>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<vector<long long>> pts(n, vector<long long>(2));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n            cin >> pts[i][j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[][] pts = new long[(int) n][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < pts.length; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < pts[i].length; j++) {\n                pts[i][j] = Long.parseLong(next());\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["For each centre the other points are grouped by squared distance. A group of `c` points gives `c * (c - 1)` ordered pairs."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2) on average, space O(n).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\npts = [list(map(int, input().split())) for _ in range(n)]\n\ntotal = 0\nfor i in range(n):\n    xi, yi = pts[i]\n    d = {}\n    for j in range(n):\n        if j != i:\n            dist = (pts[j][0] - xi) ** 2 + (pts[j][1] - yi) ** 2\n            d[dist] = d.get(dist, 0) + 1\n    for c in d.values():\n        total += c * (c - 1)\nprint(total)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <unordered_map>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<vector<long long>> pts(n, vector<long long>(2));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {\n            cin >> pts[i][j];\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long total = 0;\n    unordered_map<long long, long long> d;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        d.clear();\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            if (j == i) continue;\n            long long dx = pts[j][0] - pts[i][0], dy = pts[j][1] - pts[i][1];\n            d[dx * dx + dy * dy]++;\n        }\n        for (auto& entry : d) total += entry.second * (entry.second - 1);\n    }\n    cout << total << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[][] pts = new long[(int) n][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i < pts.length; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < pts[i].length; j++) {\n                pts[i][j] = Long.parseLong(next());\n            }\n        }\n\n        long total = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            Map<Long, Long> d = new HashMap<>();\n            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n                if (j == i) continue;\n                long dx = pts[j][0] - pts[i][0], dy = pts[j][1] - pts[i][1];\n                d.merge(dx * dx + dy * dy, 1L, Long::sum);\n            }\n            for (long c : d.values()) total += c * (c - 1);\n        }\n        System.out.println(total);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"3\n0 0\n1 0\n2 0\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"1\n5 5\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"2\n0 0\n10000 10000\n","output":"0\n"},{"input":"8\n0 -3\n-2 2\n0 2\n3 -1\n1 3\n-1 1\n-1 -1\n0 3\n","output":"16\n"},{"input":"100\n0 -6\n1 -4\n-6 6\n3 -8\n3 -6\n-8 2\n0 -3\n2 -7\n-8 -4\n-7 -4\n3 1\n3 -5\n4 -8\n1 -7\n-5 -5\n0 8\n7 6\n7 -3\n-5 -2\n-5 4\n4 -6\n-7 -8\n4 2\n-1 4\n-6 2\n0 4\n6 8\n3 4\n-5 -4\n-6 -2\n-6 -8\n7 5\n6 -3\n8 -4\n5 0\n7 -7\n-7 6\n-1 8\n-3 1\n-4 2\n-4 3\n-3 -4\n6 6\n0 3\n2 4\n-1 -2\n8 0\n8 -2\n-7 1\n-7 -7\n-3 7\n4 8\n-4 -7\n-5 2\n-1 7\n-5 7\n-2 -5\n-7 5\n-5 -6\n1 7\n7 1\n-7 0\n1 3\n-5 5\n8 -3\n-8 8\n-3 -2\n-5 1\n2 5\n6 -4\n5 2\n-1 -5\n5 -4\n0 1\n7 -1\n5 4\n-1 3\n-8 -3\n-4 -8\n8 -7\n-4 -2\n4 5\n2 -5\n-2 7\n8 2\n6 3\n-8 -5\n0 -4\n1 -2\n1 8\n5 6\n7 -2\n-8 0\n-4 -6\n-7 4\n-4 4\n1 -1\n3 6\n-6 5\n7 0\n","output":"10190\n"},{"input":"300\n6261 -3029\n-1497 9670\n6844 5001\n934 5997\n8991 5968\n-4095 -3349\n-8964 -2601\n7342 -4591\n-5155 9873\n-5442 6886\n-1554 -2976\n1134 -2677\n-9879 5921\n-1131 -5270\n-7504 9836\n-5505 2472\n-6425 -3375\n-199 657\n-3589 423\n-8587 -9108\n-6042 -2923\n-4085 -6876\n9488 3831\n-5879 8799\n3256 -4737\n450 9651\n9105 -7026\n220 -8644\n-3408 -1260\n1663 -8854\n-2648 590\n-7059 3581\n-2621 -695\n-3300 227\n-7261 -5515\n6467 6541\n-9162 267\n6258 5121\n9455 -4227\n4623 3315\n-823 6491\n-3142 -8279\n9166 7899\n2725 -2885\n1793 -6558\n-3751 6804\n-1723 318\n2614 74\n6395 -2317\n5281 3360\n2657 3200\n3874 2568\n4784 2354\n6827 -579\n-7310 9385\n9914 3384\n-667 1748\n3561 -6784\n-6279 2154\n-7779 7101\n9788 833\n3188 3100\n3187 -4064\n4711 5310\n9338 -1663\n894 6569\n-3288 -2168\n1635 -1824\n2954 5433\n-4827 3259\n5327 -4028\n5873 -4095\n-510 1241\n4556 2399\n-2587 -9257\n4308 1883\n-2575 -9992\n8903 7004\n-2038 4583\n-426 8793\n7379 -4697\n-4620 4521\n-4040 -206\n6764 2